# The match seed. One integer, or the word `random`.
#
# Everything random in a match descends from it through named streams -- the dunes,
# which engineer is hurt when ground is lost, which plane a scout's report reaches
# first -- so the same seed and the same commands produce the same match, tick for
# tick, on every machine in it. That is not a convenience; it is what lets other
# players' machines run the same match instead of being told about it.
#
# `random` draws a fresh one each run and writes it to the append-only notebook at
# tmp/shared-memory/seeds.log, so a match worth keeping can be got back afterwards by
# copying its seed in here. A seed named on the command line -- SDC_SEED -- beats both
# and is not logged, because a seed you typed is one you already have.
random
